course: dictionary
lesson: 10186
title: Tilt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To tilt something is to move it so that one side is higher than the other. It leans or slopes. «The picture is on a tilt» means the picture hangs at a slant, not straight.
explain: You tilt your head to listen, tilt a glass to pour, or tilt a chair back. Tilt can also be a noun, meaning a sloping position or a lean.
explain: Scientists use tilt for the Earth. «The Earth's axis is tilted» means our planet leans as it turns. This tilt is what makes the seasons, not how far away we are from the Sun.
fact: To tilt means to move so that one side is higher, or to lean and slope.
fact: Tilt can be a verb (tilt, tilts, tilted, tilting) or a noun (a tilt).
fact: «The Earth's axis is tilted by about 23.4 degrees.»
fact: The Earth's tilt causes the seasons. «Winter is cold because the Earth is tilted.»
fact: In a nosebleed, do not tilt your head back, because blood runs down your throat and can make you sick.
exercise: What does tilt mean? | To wash your hands carefully | *To lean or slope, so one side is higher | To shout loudly | To move so that one side is higher, or to lean
exercise: «Winter is cold because the Earth is tilted, so the light comes in low and slanted.» What does slanted mean here? | Upside down | *Sloping, not straight | Very bright | Wet
exercise: Find and copy the word that shows the Earth leans. | *tilted | days | equator | summer
test: What does the Earth's tilt cause? | Earthquakes | Thunder | *The seasons | Rainbows
test: «To tilt a glass to pour» means you | Shake it hard | Put it on a high shelf | Fill it to the very top | *Lean it so the drink flows out
exam: Which sentence uses tilt as a noun? | You tilt your head to listen | Tilting the mirror slowly | *The picture is on a tilt | The ladder will tilt over
